{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9423e61c-bcaf-4d3e-9e0d-9ff9b0cdf3e4","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have updated [`deploy.sh`](file:///tmp/h-ATUDSB/deploy.sh) to ensure that deleted files from `site/` and deleted or privatized notes/author pages are removed from S3 without causing downtime during deploys. I have also documented what was done and analyzed the colleague's note in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-ATUDSB/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes in `deploy.sh`:\n\n1. **Delete obsolete static files without dropping live pages:**\n   Updated [`sync_site`](file:///tmp/h-ATUDSB/deploy.sh#L14-L17) to include `--delete` while excluding the generated prefixes:\n   ```bash\n   aws s3 sync \"$ROOT/site/\" \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --exclude \"s/*\" --exclude \"a/*\" --only-show-errors\n   ```\n2. **In-place overwrite:**\n   Kept [`upload_pages`](file:///tmp/h-ATUDSB/deploy.sh#L19-L27) using `aws s3 cp` with explicit content-type (`text/html; charset=utf-8`) and caching headers, ensuring existing pages remain live until replaced.\n3. **Clean up stale note and author pages:**\n   Added [`clean_stale_pages`](file:///tmp/h-ATUDSB/deploy.sh#L29-L33) right after `upload_pages`:\n   ```bash\n   aws s3 sync \"$ROOT/.build/pages/s/\" \"s3://$BUCKET/s/\" --delete --only-show-errors\n   aws s3 sync \"$ROOT/.build/pages/a/\" \"s3://$BUCKET/a/\" --delete --only-show-errors\n   ```\n\n### What Applied from Colleague's Note:\n- **Applied:**\n  - Excluding generated prefixes (`s/*` and `a/*`) from the main `sync --delete` to avoid transient 404 windows during deployment.\n  - Retaining in-place overwrites with `aws s3 cp` so live pages remain served until new builds overwrite them.\n  - Adding a post-upload cleanup sync with `--delete` on the generated prefixes to delete stale pages no longer produced by the build.\n  - Using `--delete` on the main `site/` sync to clean up files removed from `site/`.\n- **Did Not Apply:**\n  - Worklore-specific paths (`paths/`). In this codebase, only `s/` and `a/` prefixes are generated.\n  - Listing bucket objects via `aws s3api list-objects-v2` and manual deletion. The colleague noted running `aws s3 sync ... --delete` after upload achieves the same result more simply and reliably.\n","duration_seconds":132.14693,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":148953,"output_tokens":3578,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":407549,"total_tokens":152531}}}
